            'inj.helpInlet': 'Orifice inlet geometry. A radiused inlet (r/d >= 0.15) raises Cd to about 0.90-0.92; a sharp edge gives 0.63-0.84 and can hydraulically flip.',
            'inj.helpLd': 'Orifice length-to-diameter ratio. It selects the discharge coefficient from the circuit C_d table (inlet type and L/D) and the hydraulic-flip verdict. Hybrid: empty means the circuit default L/D = 4 is used and no flip verdict is issued.',
            'inj.helpMdotFuel': 'Fuel mass flow rate (liquid engines only). Set by the mixture ratio: mdot_fuel = mdot_ox / (O/F).',
            'inj.helpMdotOx': 'Oxidizer mass flow rate through the injector. Typical amateur/university range 0.1-5 kg/s.',
            'inj.helpPfeed': 'Injector inlet pressure P_1 (bar, absolute). Empty: self-pressurised N2O takes P_sat(T_tank), other oxidizers P_c·(1 + dP/P_c). Filled after a calculation only when the main design uses a user-supplied tank pressure.',
            'inj.helpCd': 'Measured discharge coefficient of the orifices. Empty: C_d comes from the circuit table (inlet + L/D). Not applied to swirl elements, whose C_d follows from their geometry.',
            'inj.helpShHoles': 'Number of showerhead orifices. Empty: the circuit plans the fewest holes inside the diameter band.',
            'inj.helpN2o': 'Self-pressurised nitrous oxide flashes across the orifice. With this enabled the Dyer NHNE two-phase model sets the flow rate and the pressure drop follows from tank temperature.',
            'inj.helpPc': 'Chamber pressure at the design point. Hybrids typically 15-40 bar, liquids 30-150 bar.',
            'inj.helpRhoFuel': 'Liquid fuel density. RP-1 about 810 kg/m3, ethanol about 789 kg/m3.',
            'inj.helpRhoOx': 'Liquid oxidizer density at injection temperature. N2O at 293 K is about 745-790 kg/m3; LOX about 1141 kg/m3.',
            'inj.helpTheta': 'Target spray cone HALF-angle of the swirl elements, met through the Giffen-Muraszew inverse (K -> X -> θ). The solvable envelope is 3.7-71.2 deg: a hybrid design outside it is rejected; the liquid panel clamps it to the envelope with a warning.',
            'inj.helpTmr': 'Pintle total momentum ratio target. TMR = 1 gives a 60 deg spray half angle (Cheng 2017); usual band 0.5-2.',
            'inj.helpTox': 'Nitrous oxide tank temperature. Sets saturation pressure (about 50 bar at 293 K) and therefore the available dP.',
            'inj.helpType': 'Injector element family. Drives the geometry model, the discharge-coefficient basis and the atomisation correlation.',
            'inj.impingeAngle': 'Impingement half angle',
            'inj.inletRadiused': 'Radiused',
            'inj.inletSharp': 'Sharp edge',
            'inj.intro': 'Orifice sizing (mdot = Cd·A·sqrt(2·rho·dP)), Dyer NHNE two-phase model for N2O, element-specific geometry (impingement angle and momentum, pintle TMR/BF, swirl K to cone angle), SMD atomisation estimate, manifold sizing and chug stability checks. Sources: NASA SP-8089, Dyer 2007, Lefebvre.',
            'inj.roleWhatIf': 'Independent what-if calculator. After each main calculation it is filled from the injector circuit of that design (same type, oxidizer flow, chamber pressure, density, tank temperature, L/D, pressure drop and element inputs) and run once, so it shows the circuit numbers of the design above. Change any field to explore an alternative; the main design is not changed.',
